    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by a high-upside core of **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21), **Josh Naylor** (76.00), and **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90). **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains our strongest play as he faces Chandler, benefiting from an elite SP skill matchup (+19%) and a favorable platoon profile (+14%). **Josh Naylor** similarly thrives against Quintana, leveraging a park factor boost (+14%) and a soft matchup to climb well above his base projection. Meanwhile, **Seiya Suzuki** provides the day's most intriguing matchup upside; despite facing the southpaw Lodolo, he boasts a rare BvP edge (+8%) developed over 28 plate appearances, cementing his status as a must-start despite the handedness disadvantage.\n\nOur pursuit of stolen bases remains central to the lineup construction, though we have navigated some volatility. **Mickey Moniak** (71.33) is an essential start for speed, bolstered by a significant +14% platoon boost and an 88% stolen base success rate against the opposing pitcher\u2019s delivery. Conversely, **Jose Caballero** (51.38) sits in the marginal tier today; while his speed is vital, he is dragged down by a poor spot in the order (-8%) and a tough dynamic platoon adjustment (-13%) against Pfaadt. The most difficult bench decision involved **Austin Riley** (57.80), who narrowly missed the cut. While his underlying metrics against Wesneski are solid, the density of high-efficiency starts from **Isaac Paredes** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** forced him out of the primary lineup; **Austin Riley** remains the primary contingency should a late lineup scratch occur elsewhere.\n\nWe must monitor the health of our depth, as **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, and **Brice Turang** remain unavailable due to injury or benching, limiting our flexibility for late-game defensive substitutions. Additionally, **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll** face the significant challenge of Schlittler, whose sub-3.00 xERA creates a daunting matchup. Both players have seen their scores deflated by -19% due to the opposing SP skill, making them \"strong\" starts rather than elite ones. We are counting on the volume of our high-efficiency hitters to carry the Roto categories while accepting the risks posed by elite arms.",
